WEBVTT

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.340
Yes!

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:10.650
15-love.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:12.560
Coach Miura!

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.410
Nat-chan's winning, huh?

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:17.860
Yeah, by a long shot.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:21.410
Nakajo-san is the one she had a 
hard time with before, right?

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:25.120
Yeah. Early on, people were saying 
that if Natsu lost at Kanto,

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.420
Takasaki Natsu 
Nakajo Megumi

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.420
Nakajo would be the one to win,

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.390
but it's been a one-sided 
match from the start.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.170
I'd heard she was in top form,

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:33.730
but this is amazing.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:34.740
30-love.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:38.680
The power of love certainly is amazing.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:39.400
Huh?!

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.840
You said it.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.390
Wh-What does that mean?!

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:45.690
Oh, I'm being completely serious.

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:49.290
Since she announced that she was dating you,

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:51.690
Natsu's strength has been unreal.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:57.210
But Mike said romance mode and combat 
mode are on opposite ends of the spectrum.

00:00:57.210 --> 00:01:02.080
If that's true, it just means that 
kind of logic doesn't apply to Natsu.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:07.090
Actually, Mike did say that she had 
ingenious mental fortitude, too.

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:12.900
<i>I won!</i>

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:21.410
It's fun striving for the same goal in the 
sport she likes, with the guy she likes.

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:22.720
Thus, she plays well.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.420
From Natsu's perspective, 
it must be only natural.

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:29.850
But somehow, when it comes to us men,

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:33.480
we think of them as two separate things.

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:38.110
Even though we'd be better 
off making it work for us...

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:41.250
We could learn a lot from Natsu.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.120
That's true.

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:47.370
She really has the ability to make 
your very existence her strength.

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:51.160
So come watch her matches 
whenever you have time, okay?

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.380
O-Okay.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:54.880
Maybe I'm not one to talk, but...

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:59.410
You two are a good match. 
You have a good influence on each other.

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:00.890
R-Really?

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.290
<i>If I have something to do with that strength,</i>

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:05.890
<i>then maybe it's true.</i>

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:11.900
<i>And if that's the case, then she's been 
inspiring me since the day we met.</i>

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:16.430
<i>The strength in her eyes and 
her vibrant expressions</i>

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:18.950
<i>changed everything I'd ever believed in.</i>

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:23.300
<i>I think I was already drawn to her then,</i>

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:25.320
<i>and I've been pursuing her all this time.</i>

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:29.110
<i>If that's making Nat-chan strong now,</i>

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:31.190
<i>then I can give her all 
the strength she needs.</i>

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:36.540
<i>I want to live a life of the tennis 
I like with the person I like, too.</i>

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:39.910
<i>If I could turn these feelings 
into my strength on the court,</i>

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:41.370
<i>I bet I'd be amazing.</i>

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:49.600
Game, set, and match.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:53.310
Winner: Takasaki. Score: 6-2, 6-1.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:53.310
Takasaki Natsu 
Nakajo Megumi

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:32.000
Existence is the Driving Force

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:38.000
Ei-chan!

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:39.700
Great game.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.380
We both made it to the semifinal!

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:47.140
It's amazing that you beat 
so many seeded players!

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:48.950
Y-Yeah, I managed.

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.580
Mine were all down to the wire, though.

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:52.890
That's fine!

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:56.050
Watching your match today...

00:04:57.450 --> 00:05:00.150
I was thinking that I want to be like you.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:04.650
You already are like me.

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:05.420
Huh?

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:08.070
Because I'm already more like you!

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:09.660
H-How so?

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:12.660
Well, like... I'm more humble?

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:14.190
You are not!

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:16.180
I'm kidding. I meant my tennis.

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:17.690
Okay, I'm heading to the main office.

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:18.420
Okay...

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:20.740
<i>Is that really true?</i>

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:21.760
Did you see that?

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:24.040
Wow, I didn't know Takasaki-san had a boyfriend.

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:26.890
Takasaki Natsu and... Who's the plain-looking kid?

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:26.890
They were so lovey-dovey!

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:27.670
That's Maruo.

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:29.240
That's what you get for showing off.

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:31.380
W-We weren't showing off!

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:35.930
<i>This concludes today's matches.</i>

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:38.940
<i>Event staff, please meet at the main office.</i>

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:43.610
<i>Nabae-kun...</i>

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:46.650
It looks like Nabae-kun is practicing.

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:48.470
I'll catch up after I watch for a bit.

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:49.200
Okay.

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:58.710
<i>How are his movements so fluid and efficient?</i>

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:00.210
Nabae-kun!

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:02.540
I brought a racket for you.

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:05.550
<i>A racket? Who's that guy?</i>

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:10.210
<i>He has all those rackets already.</i>

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:12.100
<i>Does he need another one?</i>

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:12.850
Hey.

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:16.260
Way to go, Maruo. I heard 
you made the top four.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:18.600
Thanks. Same to you.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:22.550
Studying for your match against 
Nabae? You never quit, huh?

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:24.570
I wouldn't call it studying.

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:27.880
I've hardly been able to watch him play 
since the tournament started, is all.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:31.120
But it looks like he's talking 
to someone about rackets.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:34.110
Oh, he'll be at it for a while, then.

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:35.370
Huh? Why?

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:39.550
That guy is from the company that 
makes the rackets Nabae uses.

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:42.550
Nabae's unbelievably particular 
about rackets, you know.

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:43.630
Oh...

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:46.260
When you get to be a veteran at nationals,

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:48.880
manufacturers will sometimes 
lend you their rackets,

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:51.440
under the condition that 
you agree to give feedback

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:53.710
that they can use toward 
development of their product.

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:55.140
Really?

00:06:55.570 --> 00:07:02.110
Nabae gives really detailed feedback about 
the weight, balance, and string tension.

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:06.150
The manufacturers say his feedback is really 
interesting and useful for their development.

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:09.190
So apparently, most of the rackets he uses

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:12.810
were essentially engineered specifically for him.

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:14.240
Wow...

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:15.850
It was a long time ago,

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:19.410
but when he and I went to the national 
team selection training camp,

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:23.170
he had a string break while I was playing him.

00:07:23.450 --> 00:07:27.170
Sorry, this is the only racket I 
brought today, so the match is over.

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:30.690
Huh? Stick around. I'll lend you one of mine.

00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:32.510
Nah, I'll pass.

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:34.820
Why? Don't be so stuck-up.

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:37.180
I can't play with someone else's racket.

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:38.730
It throws me off.

00:07:38.730 --> 00:07:41.190
Huh? Aren't you too sensitive?

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:45.200
Maybe, but when I go back to my own racket,

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:46.940
it still feels weird for a while.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:50.940
It's not as if rackets have nerves.

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:53.520
That makes it sound like it's his own hand.

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:55.950
Well, I guess it's something similar to that.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:58.650
<i>But I can sort of understand.</i>

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:02.360
<i>Watching Nabae-kun's fluid, 
delicate use of the racket,</i>

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:05.280
<i>regulating his rackets the same way 
he regulates his physical condition</i>

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:07.110
<i>doesn't seem unnatural.</i>

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:07.960
Well...

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:11.760
Let's both kick some butt as fellow 
Kanagawa players tomorrow.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:13.470
You're playing Okada-kun, right?

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:17.780
That's gonna be a pretty 
tough match too, you know.

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:22.230
I won't feel better until I take 
my revenge on Okada by force.

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:25.980
And I believe we'll have a repeat 
of the Kanagawa final after that.

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:28.980
Be ready.

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:30.100
Sure...

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:34.000
<i>That's right. If I beat Nabae-kun, 
I'll be in the final—</i>

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:36.030
Wh-What?

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:39.010
By the way, I happened to hear earlier...

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:40.010
Yeah?

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:43.060
Are you really going out with Takasaki Natsu?

00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:45.750
<i>What?! Even Araya-kun knows about that?!</i>

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:47.400
Seriously?

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:50.770
Incredible.

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:53.250
Huh?

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:06.120
Planning your anti-Nabae strategy?

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:12.180
Yeah. But Nabae-kun can change his 
play style depending on his opponent.

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:14.460
Power, speed, technique...

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:16.780
He's a high-level player in all those.

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:19.020
When I played him in November,

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:21.840
he widened the point gap between us 
with a control-based play style.

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:27.750
Then at the end, he switched to a risky 
power-based style to finish me off.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:26.520
Maruo            Egawa            Kanda
Eiichiro          Takuma         Hisashi

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:26.520
Mental Fortitude 

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:27.750
