00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:16.110
Maruo Eiichiro

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:16.110
Is that data on Maruo?

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:21.040
He's changed a lot since
I played him, so I'm revising it.

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:22.110
Looks that way.

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:27.530
He uses flat, spin, and slice strokes, 
with variations in speed.

00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:30.670
At critical moments, he'll move up to the net,

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:33.130
and he'll serve and volley 
as well as use return dashes.

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:35.810
And he uses all that to change up the pace,

00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:37.880
which throws our timing off.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:39.990
What's important to watch for is

00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:43.370
his precise control and strong mental 
fortitude when he does that.

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:47.890
Yeah, after all I did, it'd be normal 
to get pissed, but he didn't.

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:52.390
I guess it's his personality. 
I'm not sure if he's optimistic or dense.

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:55.490
But he comes by his mental strength naturally.

00:11:56.100 --> 00:11:57.400
Unlike you.

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:02.050
Love-30.

00:12:03.830 --> 00:12:04.910
Again?

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:06.920
There he goes again.

00:12:08.130 --> 00:12:10.830
That habit of losing his temper 
when things don't go his way.

00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:14.880
He normally has far more self-discipline 
than you'd expect of a ten-year-old,

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:15.920
but in matches...

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:20.920
Nabae Yu

00:12:22.730 --> 00:12:24.930
Yu, let's go.

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:31.770
Listen, even adults can't keep their 
emotions under control all the time.

00:12:32.290 --> 00:12:35.080
Not everything will always go the way you want.

00:12:36.170 --> 00:12:41.300
But you have a stronger will 
than anyone else I know.

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:45.410
If you use that to your advantage, 
you'll be stronger than anyone.

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:50.410
You should be able to control a match, 
at least, with the strength of your will.

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:55.040
Even if you're in pain, angry, or exhausted,

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:59.630
be a player who can calmly come up with 
the best strategy in any situation.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:04.520
I believe you can become a player 
with such an invincible will.

00:13:09.370 --> 00:13:10.570
What's that?

00:13:10.570 --> 00:13:11.820
A self-analysis.

00:13:12.260 --> 00:13:14.060
Self-analysis?

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:16.710
I use it to evaluate my own play.

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:18.400
Evaluate, huh...

00:13:22.590 --> 00:13:23.560
Game, set.

00:13:24.920 --> 00:13:28.900
The fifth game... right here... I did this...

00:13:28.900 --> 00:13:32.040
You can let it out all you want now.

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:35.540
You did a good job holding it in on the court.

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:38.170
Out.

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:40.690
Game: Egawa. 2-0.

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:57.450
Is it just natural?

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:00.900
Maruo-kun has a strong will.

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:06.430
He must've done everything possible since 
our match last year, without compromise.

00:14:06.870 --> 00:14:09.610
I can really relate to him in that sense.

00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:12.830
Your tennis and his are a lot alike, somehow.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:17.080
<i>He started tennis in high school.</i>

00:14:18.150 --> 00:14:22.380
<i>I haven't seen anyone improve this quickly 
since Takuma-kun in middle school,</i>

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:25.450
<i>or Araya and Okada after 
they started high school.</i>

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.520
<i>Ide's been impressive lately too,</i>

00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:31.000
<i>but none of them hold a candle 
to Maruo-kun right now.</i>

00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:32.830
<i>And there's...</i>

00:14:33.460 --> 00:14:34.710
Oh, right.

00:14:34.710 --> 00:14:37.640
Maruo-kun's the biggest shocker since Ike Soji.

00:14:39.970 --> 00:14:41.590
When I think of it that way...

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:43.910
<i>I don't want to lose.</i>

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:47.020
Whoa, scary!

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:47.920
What?

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:50.410
It was like you flipped a switch just now.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:52.070
Really?

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:55.410
I told you, it's true!

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:58.040
I'm in the top four now.

00:14:58.040 --> 00:14:59.210
<i>Now, wait a minute...</i>

00:14:59.770 --> 00:15:03.210
Isn't it incredible to be one of 
the top four players in Kanto?

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:09.080
Yeah. Even I never thought 
I'd come this far this fast.

00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:12.120
<i>You really have gotten stronger.</i>

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:16.260
<i>But still, the stronger you get, 
the more I worry.</i>

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:18.260
Worry? Why?

00:15:18.260 --> 00:15:20.710
<i>I'm your mother. It's what I do.</i>

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:25.510
B-But anyway, I'm facing the number 
one player in Japan tomorrow.

00:15:25.510 --> 00:15:27.450
And if I win...

00:15:27.450 --> 00:15:29.250
<i>Number one in Japan?</i>

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:31.510
But will this boy

00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:34.600
<i>be able to make a living for himself as a pro?</i>

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:36.080
Yes, he will!

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:40.640
Almost everyone who made it that 
far as a junior is a pro now,

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:45.090
or if not, they're still thriving 
in some tennis-related job.

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:46.630
<i>I see...</i>

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:48.340
<i>Then...</i>

00:15:48.850 --> 00:15:51.160
<i>If you really do beat him,</i>

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:55.500
<i>maybe I'll believe that you really 
should continue to play tennis.</i>

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:57.670
Really?!

00:15:57.670 --> 00:16:00.600
<i>And if you do, I'll come watch you play.</i>

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:02.690
<i>If the final is the day after 
tomorrow, I can make it.</i>

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:03.350
Okay!

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:08.360
In Call 

00:16:03.830 --> 00:16:08.360
<i>But is there really a chance you can beat him?</i>

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:16.870
Uh...

00:16:17.430 --> 00:16:20.550
<i>Against Nabae-kun, I'll most 
likely need 1/100 control</i>

00:16:20.550 --> 00:16:23.730
<i>at critical moments, even if it's risky.</i>

00:16:23.730 --> 00:16:28.170
<i>Even when it's not critical, I'll have 
to set the pace with 1/64 control.</i>

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:29.880
<i>Interesting.</i>

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:35.070
<i>I learned last year that I'll 
lose if I don't do that much.</i>

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:37.390
Oh... Coach Aoi.

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:41.390
How do you think I can beat Nabae-kun?

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:45.400
What's this about? You getting scared now?

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:48.810
No, but you know, Nabae-kun's pretty flawless.

00:16:48.810 --> 00:16:50.320
He has no weaknesses.

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:54.450
So I think I'll have to take 
more risks than usual,

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:57.330
but I don't want to take too 
many and dig my own grave.

00:16:57.330 --> 00:16:59.980
I'm not sure what situations 
would be best to make my move.

00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:03.270
Like, in the first set of our match last year...

00:17:04.570 --> 00:17:06.960
You really seem to be enjoying this.

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:09.560
Y-You think so?

00:17:10.010 --> 00:17:13.970
I wonder why. Because I've made it 
into the All-Japan now, maybe?

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:18.110
I just feel really strongly that 
I want to play against Nabae-kun,

00:17:18.110 --> 00:17:21.470
VS Nabae Yu

00:17:18.110 --> 00:17:21.470
so I get really excited just 
thinking about tomorrow.

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:24.980
I'm taking this too easy! 
I need to shape up!

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:27.730
No, I think that's fine.

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:28.520
Huh?

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:30.330
Remember what you learned in your match?

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:33.740
It's best if your pressure level 
is neither too high nor too low.

00:17:34.100 --> 00:17:38.890
That probably means you're already beyond 
pressure, in the "challenge" mental state.

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:42.330
You should remember how that feels.

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:43.750
Really?

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:45.140
While you're at it,

00:17:45.140 --> 00:17:49.000
you might as well do something bold 
that you'd never do under pressure.

00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:51.320
L-Like what?

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:56.600
Like aiming for the lines instead of 
dividing up the court into squares.

00:17:56.600 --> 00:18:00.260
The lines? Wouldn't that 
be an unnecessary risk?

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:02.800
You can't know until you try!

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:05.020
And aim for aces on all your serves!

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:06.590
Are you serious?

00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:11.070
Well, at this point, whether you 
win or not is all up to luck.

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:12.520
If you're going to say that...

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:16.560
If you're going to be bold, 
it means nothing if you're careless.

00:18:16.560 --> 00:18:19.780
You've got to use your own experiences, 
and what makes you you.

00:18:22.050 --> 00:18:24.290
Such as... you know.

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:27.290
Huh? That?!

00:18:28.090 --> 00:18:29.150
What?!

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:36.900
Nabae Yu

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:41.300
Takagi Sakuya

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:41.300
Maruo Eiichiro

00:18:41.630 --> 00:18:44.930
Number 30, Maruo Eiichiro.

00:18:52.330 --> 00:18:53.970
<i>It is 10:00.</i>

00:18:53.970 --> 00:18:58.950
<i>The Kanto Junior Tennis Tournament 
semifinal round will now begin.</i>

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:03.090
<i>Players, please enter your designated 
court and begin warm-ups.</i>

00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:02.450
All right!

00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:13.900
<i>But is there really a chance you can beat him?</i>

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:20.260
<i>If I use everything I've done up to now,</i>

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:23.580
<i>there is a chance I can win!</i>

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:28.730
Nat-chan?

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:32.500
Hey, when this tournament's over, 
let's go somewhere together!

00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:33.210
Huh?!

00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:35.650
We'll have a break before the All-Japan.

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:37.160
Let's go out then!

00:19:37.160 --> 00:19:38.100
Huh?

00:19:38.630 --> 00:19:39.610
On a date!

00:19:41.070 --> 00:19:44.800
Matches are tough, so we need something 
to look forward to afterwards!

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:46.540
Where's this coming from?

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:49.830
But I want to have as much fun as we can,

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:52.270
so be sure to beat Nabae-kun!

00:19:57.340 --> 00:20:00.740
<i>I-I'm happy, but why now?</i>

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:03.590
<i>My combat mode is gonna 
turn into romance mode.</i>

00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:06.350
<i>Actually, I guess not.</i>

00:20:06.350 --> 00:20:10.100
<i>What is this? It's not so much 
romance mode as... happiness mode?</i>

00:20:11.780 --> 00:20:13.100
You already are like me.

00:20:14.150 --> 00:20:16.110
<i>Like Nat-chan was saying...</i>

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:20.360
<i>Is she really becoming my strength, too?</i>

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:22.520
<i>That'd be nice...</i>

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:27.870
<i>Huh? The court feels smaller, somehow.</i>

00:20:28.510 --> 00:20:32.220
<i>The first time I played here, it felt huge.</i>

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:39.560
<i>Yeah. I'm calmer than I thought I'd be.</i>

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:42.880
<i>And my body feels lighter than I expected.</i>

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:45.390
<i>I feel driven, but not stressed.</i>

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:49.300
<i>Last year, I ended up losing 
by hitting out of bounds.</i>

00:20:49.300 --> 00:20:53.180
<i>But that was the ref's mistake. 
It was actually in.</i>

00:20:53.710 --> 00:20:58.560
<i>My mental state then was good enough 
that I thought I had a chance to win.</i>

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:01.820
<i>I need to bring that state back 
to reality through my notes,</i>

00:21:02.850 --> 00:21:06.820
<i>so I can start the match 
with that same mentality.</i>

00:21:07.860 --> 00:21:12.580
The Kanto Junior Tennis Tournament 
semifinal round will now begin.

00:21:13.140 --> 00:21:17.580
<i>I'm the challenger, so I just have to 
hit him with everything I've learned!</i>

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:20.840
Three-set match. Nabae to serve.

00:21:22.580 --> 00:21:23.340
<i>A wide slice!</i>

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:25.760
<i>His shots really are sharp!</i>

00:21:26.020 --> 00:21:27.060
<i>There it is already!</i>

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:28.400
<i>But it's my return game.</i>

00:21:28.400 --> 00:21:30.010
<i>1/81!</i>

00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:34.520
Love-15.

00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:35.200
Yes!

00:21:35.200 --> 00:21:37.350
Whoa, this is already amazing!

00:21:37.350 --> 00:21:40.130
<i>I got to the ball faster than I thought,</i>

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:42.240
<i>so all my weight was behind it!</i>

00:21:42.240 --> 00:21:44.700
<i>I can hit like that when 
everything falls into place?</i>

00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:47.360
<i>Wait... Could this be...</i>

00:21:47.920 --> 00:21:50.280
<i>That wasn't like his usual shots.</i>

00:21:50.630 --> 00:21:53.540
<i>Looks like Maruo-kun is in good shape today.</i>

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:55.040
<i>No, calm down.</i>

00:21:55.430 --> 00:21:56.540
<i>Next point!</i>

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:04.090
Love-30.

00:22:05.220 --> 00:22:07.340
Nabae didn't even take a step? For real?

00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:08.500
<i>So it's true!</i>

00:22:08.980 --> 00:22:12.810
<i>Since before we started... No, since 
yesterday, something's been different.</i>

00:22:13.310 --> 00:22:16.730
<i>The court feeling small, 
getting weirdly excited...</i>

00:22:16.890 --> 00:22:21.220
<i>My mind is calm, but my body is 
responding. This feeling...</i>

00:22:23.230 --> 00:22:26.990
<i>I don't know why it's happening, 
but there's no doubt.</i>

00:22:27.600 --> 00:22:31.990
<i>I'm getting close to the zone!</i>

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:25.020
Next Time

00:24:00.500 --> 00:24:01.990
I was right!

00:24:01.990 --> 00:24:04.350
I'm focusing only on what's 
right in front of me,

00:24:04.350 --> 00:24:07.110
and nothing else is going 
through my mind at all.

00:24:07.110 --> 00:24:10.370
At a time like this, I should 
look only at his court,

00:24:10.370 --> 00:24:12.930
and leave my shots up to 
my instincts and judgment!

00:24:12.930 --> 00:24:15.590
He's close to the optimal condition 
he was in against Ide.

00:24:16.100 --> 00:24:17.850
Maruo-kun is in his best possible condition.

00:24:18.360 --> 00:24:20.430
It won't be easy to break.

00:24:20.680 --> 00:24:22.560
Next time on <i>Baby Steps</i>,

00:24:21.540 --> 00:24:25.020
Aggressive is Ideal

00:24:22.560 --> 00:24:25.020
"Aggressive is Ideal."

00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:31.000
End
